      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the number of distinct equilateral triangles in the plane of a regular nine-sided polygon \\(A_1A_2A_3A_4A_5A_6A_7A_8A_9\\) that have at least two vertices from the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of equilateral triangles in a regular polygon:**\n   For a regular \\(n\\)-sided polygon, the number of distinct equilateral triangles is given by \\(\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{6}\\). For \\(n = 9\\), the number of equilateral triangles is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7}{6} = 84.\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the equilateral triangles that do not have any vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\):**\n   An equilateral triangle in a regular nine-sided polygon does not have more than 3 vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\). The only equilateral triangles in a nine-sided polygon that have no vertices in \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\) are those with two vertices on the polygon and one vertex outside the polygon. However, since the polygon is defined completely within itself, we need to consider the in-plane equilateral triangles. The only in-plane equilateral triangles in a nine-sided polygon are those formed by vertices that are 3 steps apart (i.e., skipping one vertex at each step). These triangles are:\n   - \\(A_1A_4A_7\\)\n   - \\(A_2A_5A_8\\)\n   - \\(A_3A_6A_9\\)\n   These are the only equilateral triangles in the plane of the polygon that can be formed without including any vertices from \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\).\n\n   Therefore, the number of equilateral triangles that have no vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\) is 3.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of equilateral triangles that have at least two vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\):**\n   The total number of distinct equilateral triangles is 84. Subtracting the number of equilateral triangles that do not have any vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\) gives:\n   \\[\n   84 - 3 = 81.\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of distinct equilateral triangles in the plane of the polygon that have at least two vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\) is \\(\\boxed{81}\\).",
